WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.370
Think back to your childhood, and ask yourself:
what was the most pain you ever felt while

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.560
growing up?

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.950
As we develop, our understanding of pain evolves
according to our different experiences.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.230
The older we get, the injuries we suffered
as children like a scraped knee, or a bee

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.830
sting rarely cause us the same level of distress
as they used to.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:25.490
Of course, when you are young and unfamiliar
with sensations of pain, what you really need

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:29.820
in that moment straight after you’ve fallen
off your bike, or tripped playing soccer,

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.130
is someone to pick you back up and give your
sore spot a kiss.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:37.410
Perhaps you even need a bowl of warm soup
to comfort you.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.900
Luckily for you, SCP-348 is exactly that.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.960
While many of the anomalies held in containment
by the SCP Foundation have earned the “Euclid”

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.530
or infamous “Keter” class designations,
SCP-348 is one of the few considered to be

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:58.710
Safe - both in the sense it poses no containment
risk, and in that it wouldn’t hurt a fly.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.580
It is neither an ancient, eldritch abomination
from another dimension spreading its influence

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.050
in our world through memetic stimuli, nor
is it a recording of a basketball game in

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:11.490
which all the players and spectators are trapped
inside.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:16.750
It isn’t an indestructible, limb-regenerating
reptile, or a towering winged being, wielding

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.300
a flaming sword and guarding the entrance
to the Garden of Eden.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.330
To put it simply, SCP-348 is a bowl.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:29.270
A white ceramic bowl, the kind you would find
almost anywhere in the world.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:32.810
It may even look indistinguishable from one
in your own kitchen cabinet.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:38.159
Of course, SCP-348 is hardly as ordinary as
it outwardly appears to be.

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:42.770
And it certainly isn’t the only inanimate
object that the Foundation keeps safely stored

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:43.770
away.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:48.840
The key thing that differentiates SCP-348
from most other anomalies is how genuinely

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.530
harmless it is.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:55.200
Its anomalous properties do not cause injury
to any individual that interacts with it,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.440
nor does this bowl have any adverse effects
on the world around it.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:04.780
SCP-348 cannot bend or reshape reality, it
does not cause the person eating from it to

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:09.819
have premonitions of their own death, and
using it certainly does not manifest a contract-making

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:12.370
entity at the opposite side of the table.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:15.970
So, what makes this bowl in any way anomalous?

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:21.000
What about it categorizes it as an SCP, and
not just a harmless piece of fine crockery?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.730
Well, why don’t we start with how SCP-348
was first discovered.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:30.090
Some time ago, the SCP Foundation was made
aware of rumors surrounding a child living

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.599
in an unknown part of the world.

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:36.340
According to the intelligence gathered by
the Foundation, this child seemed to possess

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:41.450
some sort of healing ability, or at least
this is what rumors suggested.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:45.780
Upon further investigation, the source of
these so-called “remarkable recovery abilities”

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:51.370
wasn’t the child, but appeared to come from
a small ceramic bowl, which we now know as

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.099
SCP-348.

00:02:53.099 --> 00:02:58.070
This is not to say that the bowl has any inherently
supernatural healing properties, and it doesn’t

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:01.730
impart any regenerative power to those that
eat from it, either.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:06.770
It does heal in a certain sense, but not in
the way you’re probably imagining.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:12.239
When the SCP Foundation recovered SCP-348,
there were no markings on it indicating where

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:15.819
the bowl came from or who it was manufactured
by.

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:19.930
The only visually distinct details worthy
of note were flowery patterns that appeared

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:25.350
to be hand-painted around both the inside
and outside of SCP-348.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:29.739
The ceramic surface also bore the Chinese
letters 想着你.

00:03:29.739 --> 00:03:32.770
Which translates to the phrase, “thinking
of you.”

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:37.030
The child that first discovered it found the
ceramic bowl in the attic of their home.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:41.230
The child’s parents were both full-time
workers and seemed to be somewhat neglectful

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:46.200
of their child, although they refused to comment
on this, but according to the findings of

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:51.920
the SCP Foundation, the child had come to
rely on SCP-348.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:57.260
Deciding to further investigate the anomalous
properties of SCP-348, the Foundation began

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.400
testing it.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.710
Given that the child who first discovered
the bowl had relied upon it, tests involved

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:08.350
Foundation researchers presenting certain
children to SCP-348 and observing the results.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.709
So, was this bowl haunted?

00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:15.470
Perhaps harboring some malicious spirit or
entity that sought to corrupt these children,

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:19.680
maybe even healing them in order to somehow
use them as a vessel to break into our world?

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.680
No.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:25.509
And while it may not have “healed” in
any overt or expected way, it did heal in

00:04:25.509 --> 00:04:27.759
at least a metaphorical sense.

00:04:27.759 --> 00:04:32.770
If presented with an injured child, sporting
any form of minor ailment such as a cut or

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:37.270
a runny nose, SCP-348 fills with warm soup.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.120
And yes, that’s right, we said soup.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:41.229
What kind, you may ask?

00:04:41.229 --> 00:04:43.819
Well, that seems to vary.

00:04:43.819 --> 00:04:47.719
Sometimes it is tomato soup, other times it
might be chicken noodle soup.

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:52.069
While the ingredients used in its soups are
often different, there are notable consistencies

00:04:52.069 --> 00:04:54.629
to how SCP-348 heals.

00:04:54.629 --> 00:04:58.550
If anyone between the ages of four years old
and eighteen years old sits down in front

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:03.300
of the blue flowered bowl, then SCP-348 will
fill with soup.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.860
Numerous young test subjects brought in by
the Foundation to eat from this particular

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:11.539
bowl of soup have reported that they enjoyed
their meal, usually finishing the entire bowl

00:05:11.539 --> 00:05:14.249
when permitted to by research staff.

00:05:14.249 --> 00:05:19.240
Many of the injured children that were tested
have stated that the soup they eat from SCP-348

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.910
reminds them of their parents’ cooking.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:26.309
These children have expressed contentment
and feelings of comfort after acquiring their

00:05:26.309 --> 00:05:28.460
various cuts and bruises.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:33.629
Some even claimed that, even though they were
in a room all alone, they didn’t feel lonely

00:05:33.629 --> 00:05:35.310
when they were eating the soup.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:40.020
And the anomalous properties don’t end after
a child finishes the soup.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:45.469
Usually, although not always, the bowl will
leave the child a message, often some brief

00:05:45.469 --> 00:05:48.159
words of reassurance or comfort.

00:05:48.159 --> 00:05:53.089
These messages materialize on the inside rim
of the bowl, and seem to be specifically tailored

00:05:53.089 --> 00:05:55.469
to the subject that has just eaten.

00:05:55.469 --> 00:05:59.499
The words will not only be written in the
child’s first language, but are often linked

00:05:59.499 --> 00:06:03.539
to the child’s home life or relationship
with their parents.

00:06:03.539 --> 00:06:09.189
Messages that appear on SCP-348 usually fade
over time, normally disappearing after a few

00:06:09.189 --> 00:06:12.650
hours, or when the bowl refills with more
soup.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:18.300
One test of SCP-348 saw a little girl, aged
eight and suffering from a sore throat, brought

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.029
before the bowl.

00:06:20.029 --> 00:06:23.759
According to a background screening made by
research personnel, the girl lived with her

00:06:23.759 --> 00:06:29.199
biological parents, and apparently had a good
relationship with both her mother and father.

00:06:29.199 --> 00:06:34.839
When SCP-348 filled with soup for her, the
girl took almost a half hour to finish eating,

00:06:34.839 --> 00:06:38.699
and afterwards reported that she felt her
sore throat get better as she ate.

00:06:38.699 --> 00:06:43.020
By the end of the meal, this test subject
remarked that she felt completely normal.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:46.710
In this instance, no message appeared within
the bowl.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:52.939
Another child was brought in to continue the
testing of SCP-348, this time a boy of ten.

00:06:52.939 --> 00:06:57.929
Unlike the previous test, this boy was not
on good terms with his parents and often argued

00:06:57.929 --> 00:06:58.929
with them.

00:06:58.929 --> 00:07:03.669
At the time of testing, the boy had sustained
several minor bruises, the result of a small

00:07:03.669 --> 00:07:07.580
accident that had occurred while the boy had
been out riding his bike.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:12.929
Much like the little girl, this subject ate
the soup that SCP-348 presented him with.

00:07:12.929 --> 00:07:16.400
This time though, the bowl offered a message
to the boy.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:21.659
The lettering found on the ceramic surface
of SCP-348 simply read “Don’t forget to

00:07:21.659 --> 00:07:22.659
brush.”

00:07:22.659 --> 00:07:27.430
Messages also appeared when an eleven year
old boy with a slight cold ate soup from the

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:28.430
bowl.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:33.800
This child had been adopted by a foster family,
and after eating from SCP-348, he saw the

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.219
message “I’m glad you’re happy” appear.

00:07:37.219 --> 00:07:41.909
Another young test subject, a boy aged six,
had a similar experience.

00:07:41.909 --> 00:07:46.960
In this instance, the child had several scrapes
and scratches from playing with his friends.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:51.039
His parents had divorced, and he was living
with his mother at the time of testing.

00:07:51.039 --> 00:07:56.399
This time, SCP-348’s to message this boy
read “I’m sorry, son.”

00:07:56.399 --> 00:08:01.409
A seven year old girl suffering from a cough
was brought before SCP-348.

00:08:01.409 --> 00:08:06.669
She had lost her father to a traffic accident
some time before testing commenced, and received

00:08:06.669 --> 00:08:10.709
the message “I love you” after finishing
her soup.

00:08:10.709 --> 00:08:14.840
Further testing conducted by the Foundation
revealed that anyone over the age of eighteen

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:20.520
years who attempted to eat soup from SCP-348
experienced things slightly differently.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:25.189
Unlike the children, older subjects mostly
displayed a disinterest in finishing their

00:08:25.189 --> 00:08:26.189
meal.

00:08:26.189 --> 00:08:30.080
A common complaint among those over eighteen
was that the soup was “missing something.”

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:36.669
However, in a few isolated cases, testing
SCP-348 on older candidates still revealed

00:08:36.669 --> 00:08:41.620
messages, although the words seemed to be
faded, not the clear, hand-painted blue that

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:44.350
appeared when the children had finished their
soup.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:49.390
One woman, aged thirty, who was suffering
from a headache sat down in front of SCP-348.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:53.640
Much like it had done before, the bowl filled
with soup and the woman ate.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:57.910
As with some of the younger subjects, a key
aspect of this woman’s background seemed

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:00.640
to be what triggered the message to appear.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.790
Specifically, she admitted to being on bad
terms with her mother and father.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:09.030
The woman explained that she had opted to
live on her own, isolating herself from her

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.030
family.

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:14.040
In fact, she even described having rejected
an offer her father made to her many years

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:18.250
earlier, refusing some career training that
he was willing to give in order to help her

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.840
secure a job.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:24.810
When she’d finished the soup, one word appeared
in the bowl: “Why?”

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:29.950
Another woman, who was forty years old, was
also brought in for the SCP-348 testing.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:34.140
Much like the previous subject, she had moved
away from home and become estranged from her

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.810
parents over the years.

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:40.490
But unlike the previous test, this woman had
taken it upon herself to not only send money

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:44.500
to her parents, but also arranged senior care
for both as well.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.910
Prior to testing, her father had died peacefully
of natural causes after spending his last

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:52.050
days in the care that this woman had paid
for.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:56.310
As the woman ate the soup from the bowl, she
remarked about its apparently “bitter”

00:09:56.310 --> 00:10:00.180
taste, but also described her meal as “fulfilling”.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:05.440
After she had finished, the words “Thank
you” appeared within SCP-348.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:11.490
One other adult subject that produced a noticeable
result from SCP-348 was a forty year old male.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:15.550
The results of this test appeared to be the
most distinctly different from any previous

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.090
adult or child.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:22.510
By now, researchers working for the SCP Foundation
had determined that familial history seemed

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:28.800
to play an important role in the outcome of
any interaction with SCP-348, and this individual

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:31.230
was certainly different to most.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:36.650
The man in question had murdered his father
roughly a year before the testing took place.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:41.550
He began the test with SCP-348 while afflicted
with aches in his back.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:46.080
After one taste of the soup that appeared
in the bowl before him, the murderer was immediately

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.080
repulsed.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:51.430
He complained about the taste, refusing to
eat any more from SCP-348.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:55.430
Shortly after, the man began to experience
severe stomach pain.

00:10:55.430 --> 00:11:01.560
The potentially poisonous soup was disposed
of, but SCP-348 immediately filled with salt

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:05.530
water, which took three hours to disappear
from the bowl.

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:10.920
Despite conducting numerous tests with subjects
of all ages and ailments, the SCP Foundation

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:15.660
researchers have so far been unable to determine
the origins of the messages that sometimes

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.340
appear in SCP-348.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:23.170
Some have theorized, because of the family
histories of some children and adults tested,

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:28.100
that the words somehow come from the father
of whoever eats the soup, since even when

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:33.030
a subject’s father is alive or present in
their life, the message seems to convey feelings

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:36.160
that their father has, or would have.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:42.320
Other researchers claim this is just the purpose
of SCP-348, to provide comfort to small children

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:45.580
dealing with pain, both inside and out.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:51.760
And after all, isn’t providing comfort what
a good bowl of soup, anomalous or not, is

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:52.820
best at?

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:59.650
Now check out “SCP-999 - The Tickle Monster”
and “A Sea Snail's Fantasy SCP-1867 - A

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:03.040
Gentleman” for more fascinating anomalies
that mean you no harm.

